## Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

## Build output
build/
dist/
*.zip

## YOUR copy of the Weird Frontiers books. Never committed — the text is not ours to
## redistribute. See tools/corpus_paths.py, or set WF_CORPUS_DIR to point elsewhere.
corpus/
*.pdf

## EVERYTHING DERIVED FROM THE BOOKS. One rule, deliberately broad: if a generator produced it
## from the Weird Frontiers text, it is not committed. That avoids drawing fine lines about which
## derived values are "just mechanics" -- `npm run build` reproduces all of it from your corpus in
## well under a minute.
##
## Note this means a FRESH CLONE DOES NOT RUN until you build: the class, fumble and monster data
## are generated into module/, and a missing ESM import stops Foundry loading the module at all.
data/
packs/*/src/
module/wf-class-registry.mjs
module/wf-fumble-data.mjs
module/wf-monster-crit-data.mjs
templates/actor-partial-wf-common.html
templates/actor-partial-wf-equipment.html
templates/actor-partial-wf-goods.html
templates/actor-partial-wf-npc-common.html

## Compiled compendium packs. Source of truth is packs/<name>/src/*.json; the LevelDB is a
## build artifact produced by `npm run todb`.
packs/**/*.ldb
packs/**/*.log
packs/**/LOCK
packs/**/LOG*
packs/**/CURRENT
packs/**/MANIFEST*
*.lock

## Read-only upstream clones for API comparison (tools/fetch_reference.sh)
reference/

## Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

## Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

## Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
